               modern communication theory. This textbook presents
               information-theoretic methods with applications in statistical
               learning and computer science, such as f-divergences, PAC Bayes
               and variational principle, Kolmogorov's metric entropy, strong
               data processing inequalities, and entropic upper bounds for
               statistical estimation. Accompanied by a solutions manual for
